# supa registry — the one file you maintain by hand: name -> project repo root.
# Copy to `supa.registry` (same dir) and edit for your machine.
#
# Format (one per line):  name|path
#   name — the alias you type:  supa up <name>
#          letters/digits/._- only; other names are ignored (`supa doctor` lists them)
#   path — the repo root. supa finds supabase/config.toml under it (root,
#          apps/<x>/, or examples/<x>/) and reads its label + ports live.
#
# Paths: leading ~ = home dir; forward slashes on Windows (C:/code/web);
# absolute paths work. Blank lines and #-comments ignored.
# Relocate via SUPA_REGISTRY (file) or SUPA_HOME (dir).

web|~/code/web
api|~/code/api
